1
00:00:07,019 --> 00:00:19,433
[tn]: So, I wanted to ask about becoming an aryan, a sotāpanna or higher, or becoming one with the right view, or entering jhanas.

2
00:00:20,861 --> 00:00:23,456
[tn]: Are these things accidental?

3
00:00:24,813 --> 00:00:27,243
[tn]: Can you stumble into them?

4
00:00:27,661 --> 00:00:30,571
[tn]: Can you stumble into right view and then lose it?

5
00:00:31,693 --> 00:00:32,633
[nm]: Or forget about it.

6
00:00:32,630 --> 00:00:33,344
[tn]: Or forget about it.

7
00:00:33,344 --> 00:00:33,357
[tn]: Can you forget how?
[tn]: Or forget about it.

8
00:00:33,357 --> 00:00:34,944
[tn]: Can you forget how?

9
00:00:35,362 --> 00:00:36,896
[nm]: Not the slightest.

10
00:00:38,832 --> 00:00:48,907
[nm]: Otherwise, if that were the truth, we wouldn't need the Buddha and his teachings, and all the teachings he'd done, and all the instruction, and all the repetitive effort, encouragement, and everything else.

11
00:00:50,848 --> 00:00:58,987
[nm]: The Buddha wouldn't be going around saying, whatever is to be obtained by manly effort, manly dedication, manly determination, and that's what I've obtained.

12
00:00:58,982 --> 00:01:00,985
[nm]: No, he would say, oh, look, I stumbled upon this.

13
00:01:03,028 --> 00:01:04,150
[tn]: How did you do it?

14
00:01:04,656 --> 00:01:05,156
[nm]: Exactly.

15
00:01:05,156 --> 00:01:05,163
[nm]: So, if...
[nm]: Exactly.

16
00:01:05,163 --> 00:01:06,786
[nm]: So, if...

17
00:01:07,152 --> 00:01:13,298
[nm]: If it's the right understanding, you will know how you've done it, because it's knowing how to do it, means that's what the right understanding is.

18
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:17,888
[nm]: So, the right view means understanding what the right view is.

19
00:01:18,153 --> 00:01:19,131
[nm]: That's your right view.

20
00:01:20,548 --> 00:01:27,668
[nm]: It's not the experience you had that felt right, but you don't quite know what it was, or how it was, or how you came... how it came to be.

21
00:01:28,758 --> 00:01:35,081
[nm]: Same with jhana, same with any other establishment of composure in your mind and discernment, comprehension.

22
00:01:36,957 --> 00:01:40,489
[nm]: That's why the suttas would say, like, eh...

23
00:01:40,484 --> 00:01:57,890
[nm]: I think on many different occasions, but the one I'm thinking of, I think it was about Venerable Sariputta, when he was going through the various establishments of mind, through, like, discernment and reflection, he says, knowingly, these states, knowingly, these experiences have been discerned, knowingly, they were present, knowingly, those ceased.

24
00:01:58,470 --> 00:01:59,730
[tn]: Knowingly are surmounted.

25
00:01:59,730 --> 00:01:59,748
[nm]: Yes, knowingly, basically, with full understanding for their duration. Ah...
[tn]: Knowingly are surmounted.

26
00:01:59,748 --> 00:02:03,446
[nm]: Yes, knowingly, basically, with full understanding for their duration. Ah...

27
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,078
[nm]: This is. This is what this is.

28
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:07,216
[nm]: This is freedom from sensuality.

29
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:10,043
[nm]: This is freedom from, from, from ill-will.

30
00:02:10,898 --> 00:02:12,187
[nm]: Oh, this is the right view.

31
00:02:13,899 --> 00:02:15,202
[nm]: And that's, that's what Buddha said.

32
00:02:15,202 --> 00:02:20,646
[nm]: Sotāpanna, when he describes sotāpanna, I think in that Saṃyutta Nikāya, he was... Who is Sotāpanna?

33
00:02:20,646 --> 00:02:20,653
[nm]: Sotāpanna is one who knows that he knows.
[nm]: Sotāpanna, when he describes sotāpanna, I think in that Saṃyutta Nikāya, he was... Who is Sotāpanna?

34
00:02:20,653 --> 00:02:23,030
[nm]: Sotāpanna is one who knows that he knows.

35
00:02:23,824 --> 00:02:27,522
[nm]: And it's not just joking around or saying something funny.

36
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:27,792
[nm]: No.

37
00:02:27,792 --> 00:02:30,080
[nm]: That was the most accurate description.

38
00:02:30,592 --> 00:02:32,251
[nm]: He knows that he knows.

39
00:02:33,110 --> 00:02:37,942
[nm]: So, it's a reflexive knowledge upon his knowledge or full understanding.

40
00:02:40,329 --> 00:02:52,230
[nm]: It's not something happened to him that felt right and then he spent next six months trying to interpret it in a pleasing manner and then decided that he must be a sotāpanna because of that experience.

41
00:02:54,486 --> 00:02:57,762
[nm]: It's basically putting the... putting the cart in front of the horse.

42
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:09,819
[nm]: As in, through discerning what the right context is, through discerning what the right view is, you can get, then, to do it rightly, by knowing the right context.

43
00:03:10,201 --> 00:03:15,264
[nm]: But you can't accidentally do it rightly and then induce the context on account of it.

44
00:03:18,150 --> 00:03:22,617
[nm]: So, the wrong view is abandoned, not through, like, accidentally doing the right things,

45
00:03:23,830 --> 00:03:26,795
[nm]: And then you realize, oh, so this must be that right view.

46
00:03:27,654 --> 00:03:34,082
[nm]: The wrong view is abandoned through understanding what the right view is or understanding what the wrong view is, why wrong view is wrong.

47
00:03:34,749 --> 00:03:35,492
[nm]: That's what Buddha said.

48
00:03:35,819 --> 00:03:38,004
[nm]: He knows that he knows.

49
00:03:38,438 --> 00:03:42,756
[nm]: Or he said he understands skillful as skillful.

50
00:03:42,989 --> 00:03:47,899
[nm]: He understands right as right and he understands wrong as wrong.

51
00:03:49,851 --> 00:03:51,010
[nm]: He understands means

52
00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:58,582
[nm]: that context remains unchanged, imperturbable, regardless of what the experience is, on a particular level.

53
00:03:58,910 --> 00:04:11,947
[nm]: But for most people, it's the particular level experience that they're chasing, some novelty releases and energies and whatnot, and clarities of mind that occur on account of something, whatever, and then they try to read into it.

54
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:13,629
[nm]: And that's what I mean.

55
00:04:13,622 --> 00:04:15,867
[nm]: It's basically put in the second, which is the first.

56
00:04:18,235 --> 00:04:21,750
[nm]: And that's why the suttas, those who did get the right view, would say that to the Buddha.

57
00:04:22,025 --> 00:04:26,518
[nm]: Oh, it is like putting the first which should have been first.

58
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:30,546
[nm]: That which I was placed in second, you put it to be first.

59
00:04:30,546 --> 00:04:30,550
[nm]: Now I understand.
[nm]: That which I was placed in second, you put it to be first.

60
00:04:30,550 --> 00:04:31,542
[nm]: Now I understand.

61
00:04:32,192 --> 00:04:33,997
[nm]: Or turning things that have been upside down.

62
00:04:35,718 --> 00:04:37,462
[nm]: It's that perversion of the basic order.

63
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:39,133
[nm]: Me first, everything else second.

64
00:04:39,876 --> 00:04:42,432
[nm]: But you realize everything else is first, I'm second...

65
00:04:43,245 --> 00:04:44,806
[nm]: in regard to my experience as a whole.

66
00:04:45,243 --> 00:04:54,368
[nm]: So, whether you had experience that you never had before, this great release of energy, and compassion, and loving-kindness, and peace, that's absolutely fine.

67
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:57,099
[nm]: But, what is that in your experience?

68
00:04:57,364 --> 00:04:59,698
[nm]: Oh, it was just a pleasing, peaceful experience.

69
00:04:59,698 --> 00:04:59,993
[nm]: Great.

70
00:05:01,323 --> 00:05:02,836
[nm]: Is there understanding in regard to it?

71
00:05:03,449 --> 00:05:05,668
[nm]: Do I know exactly why it came to be?

72
00:05:05,773 --> 00:05:06,921
[nm]: How it came to be?

73
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:08,057
[nm]: Do I understand it?

74
00:05:08,667 --> 00:05:09,558
[nm]: That it's skillful?

75
00:05:09,723 --> 00:05:10,630
[nm]: As in, what the Buddha said:

76
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:12,340
[nm]: Do I understand skillful is skillful?

77
00:05:13,650 --> 00:05:16,310
[nm]: Or, am I just enjoying the fact that it was pleasing to me?

78
00:05:19,078 --> 00:05:27,270
[nm]: So, if there is no understanding of the nature of that state, means you are still regarding yourself as the most important thing.

79
00:05:28,406 --> 00:05:30,700
[nm]: As in, this happened to me and that's why it's special.

80
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:42,192
[nm]: But if you start putting everything in question, including the most peaceful experiences you had, you will then start questioning your own existence through that.

81
00:05:43,012 --> 00:05:48,246
[nm]: You will be refusing to place your gratuitous notion of self as the center of that experience.

82
00:05:48,710 --> 00:05:57,821
[nm]: And by that, I mean, you had a novelty peaceful experience, that was very pleasing, but then you... okay, so what is... what are the characteristics of this experience?

83
00:05:58,233 --> 00:05:59,675
[nm]: Do I know how it came about?

84
00:05:59,707 --> 00:06:00,402
[nm]: Not quite.

85
00:06:01,337 --> 00:06:02,672
[nm]: Do I know how long it will stay?

86
00:06:03,257 --> 00:06:03,986
[nm]: Not quite.

87
00:06:06,313 --> 00:06:07,691
[nm]: Do I know why is it good?

88
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:10,002
[nm]: Except that it's pleasing for me.

89
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:13,648
[nm]: Oh, am I also trying to prolong it?

90
00:06:14,310 --> 00:06:15,853
[nm]: Will I be affected if it changes?

91
00:06:16,810 --> 00:06:18,786
[nm]: Will I suffer on account of it disappearing?

92
00:06:19,718 --> 00:06:23,428
[nm]: All these things would be sort of pointing at the context you need to discern.

93
00:06:26,964 --> 00:06:27,520
[nm]: And that's the thing.

94
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:31,181
[nm]: Context is not in particular manifestation of the things.

95
00:06:31,190 --> 00:06:32,496
[nm]: It's a background of it.

96
00:06:33,433 --> 00:06:36,685
[nm]: That's why context is on the level of proper mindfulness, as we spoke before.

97
00:06:38,969 --> 00:06:49,565
[nm]: So, if all these questions, you get to realize, okay, so this peaceful state, yeah, it's obviously, it's much better, much less unwholesome than, you know, sensuality or any other types of pleasure I know.

98
00:06:49,570 --> 00:06:53,833
[nm]: But then, at the same time, it has arisen for me, in my experience.

99
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,312
[nm]: I have no control over it.

100
00:06:55,570 --> 00:06:57,910
[nm]: I don't know how it came about. I did not create it.

101
00:07:01,677 --> 00:07:03,019
[nm]: Let those questions endure.

102
00:07:03,010 --> 00:07:04,825
[nm]: Let those characteristics endure a bit.

103
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:06,699
[nm]: Don't jump at the answers or conclusions.

104
00:07:07,033 --> 00:07:09,625
[nm]: Just feel that as the state of your being.

105
00:07:09,949 --> 00:07:10,358
[nm]: Okay.

106
00:07:10,585 --> 00:07:12,363
[nm]: So, this is pleasant, but I don't know how it came about.

107
00:07:13,177 --> 00:07:21,828
[nm]: And then, naturally, you will be more cautious about... Well, you'll be more cautious in regard to losing sight of it.

108
00:07:22,690 --> 00:07:27,968
[nm]: You'll be more cautious in regard to, sort of, gratuitously, at face value, wanting it longer, protecting it.

109
00:07:29,229 --> 00:07:31,270
[nm]: Because it came to be and had nothing to do with you.

110
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:37,115
[nm]: Yeah, it's pleasing, but pleasure that came to be, has nothing to do with you.

111
00:07:37,710 --> 00:07:43,332
[nm]: In other words, if you don't lose sight of it, you're not going to get blindly attached to it, to put it simply.

112
00:07:45,702 --> 00:07:50,020
[nm]: And if you're not blindly attached to it, then you won't be gratuitously, blindly defending it.

113
00:07:51,419 --> 00:07:56,676
[nm]: Or trying to, like, squeeze the... what you read in the suttas and interpret your experience in that manner.

114
00:07:56,962 --> 00:07:57,901
[nm]: There won't be need for it.

115
00:07:58,301 --> 00:08:02,633
[nm]: If you truly understood it, you understood what the suttas talk about it on the basis of that experience.

116
00:08:02,955 --> 00:08:07,481
[nm]: But if you haven't truly understood it, that means you have to spend time tying loose ends.

117
00:08:08,164 --> 00:08:10,178
[nm]: And... and... oh, this is maybe what that meant.

118
00:08:10,347 --> 00:08:10,907
[nm]: Or not it.

119
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:17,088
[nm]: Like, at no point during that tying of loose ends do you... do you question your experience.

120
00:08:17,984 --> 00:08:21,862
[nm]: As in, that experience of novelty, of peace you had, that's it.

121
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:22,386
[nm]: That's it.

122
00:08:22,390 --> 00:08:23,206
[nm]: That's a fact.

123
00:08:23,478 --> 00:08:26,651
[nm]: Now, it's just a question of finding the right interpretation for it.

124
00:08:27,885 --> 00:08:30,834
[nm]: And what I'm saying is, that's a completely wrong way around.

125
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:37,366
[nm]: Through understanding what the right interpretation is, you get to recognize what right experiences are.

126
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:42,612
[nm]: That's why sottāpatti, or any other establishment of matters, cannot be done by accident.

127
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:45,302
[nm]: That's why you need utterance of another.

128
00:08:46,114 --> 00:08:48,416
[nm]: And faith in that, and properly attending to it.

129
00:08:48,820 --> 00:09:01,424
[nm]: Because, the utterance of , without the external criteria that you took on faith, how can you repeat something, sufficient amount of times, which is many times, without any apparent result to it?

130
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:03,307
[nm]: Why would you repeat it?

131
00:09:03,316 --> 00:09:04,297
[nm]: It's just impossible.

132
00:09:04,795 --> 00:09:06,964
[nm]: It's even, like, statistically impossible.

133
00:09:12,077 --> 00:09:24,587
[nm]: So, even in theory, unless you know that something should be repeated and adhered to, and unless you understand it, and unless you have faith in it, you cannot possibly do that sufficient amount of time, because there is no apparent result.

134
00:09:30,178 --> 00:09:33,515
[nm]: So, that's why you cannot establish any of those things accidentally.

135
00:09:34,116 --> 00:09:39,373
[nm]: And if something accidentally happens, means, yeah, it happened on the level of particular experience.

136
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:41,094
[nm]: But that's not what matters.

137
00:09:41,092 --> 00:09:42,920
[nm]: What matters is understanding of it.

138
00:09:43,090 --> 00:09:44,440
[nm]: The context I'm talking about.

139
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:47,021
[nm]: So, that's why the context comes first.

140
00:09:47,110 --> 00:09:49,254
[nm]: That's why the right view comes first.

141
00:09:49,650 --> 00:09:52,169
[nm]: The whole noble eightfold path is rooted in the right view.

142
00:09:52,164 --> 00:09:53,474
[nm]: Every single factor of it.

143
00:09:55,001 --> 00:09:56,253
[nm]: Not the other way around.

144
00:09:56,770 --> 00:10:00,886
[nm]: Not like I do this, I do this, then I do this, then I do this, then I do this, then... Oh, look!

145
00:10:00,955 --> 00:10:02,244
[nm]: I must be doing it rightly.

146
00:10:03,033 --> 00:10:07,858
[nm]: Through knowing what's doing it rightly, you get to recognize the doing of right things.

147
00:10:08,944 --> 00:10:11,300
[nm]: And that's, you know, you might even be surprised.

148
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:16,960
[nm]: What you thought was peaceful and lofty, once you develop the right context, you realize actually wasn't.

149
00:10:18,192 --> 00:10:22,966
[nm]: And things that you never kind of gave them a second look, you realize, no, that was actually closer to the right view.

150
00:10:23,510 --> 00:10:27,990
[nm]: But you can only have that criteria when you have the context that can judge that criteria from.

151
00:10:31,952 --> 00:10:37,012
[nm]: And the context is something that's understood on the basis of things you experience, not something that's read into it.

152
00:10:41,730 --> 00:10:46,726
[nm]: So, if you want to develop something, you need to have an overall picture of what you're trying to develop.

153
00:10:48,752 --> 00:10:55,769
[nm]: If you want to build something, you need to have an overall picture of what you're trying to build, and then see what matches it through your efforts.

154
00:10:57,300 --> 00:11:04,400
[nm]: Not like just start building left and right and suddenly, miraculously, becomes that thing, but you have no idea how you arrived at it.

155
00:11:06,619 --> 00:11:09,938
[nm]: How can you build a house if you don't have a notion of what house is?

156
00:11:12,683 --> 00:11:16,410
[nm]: And again, that's something, if a person were to self-question, it would become apparent.

157
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:23,597
[nm]: How can I be... How can I free myself from suffering, if I don't understand what freedom from suffering is?

158
00:11:24,377 --> 00:11:29,195
[nm]: If I just use criteria of my current feeling towards freedom of suffering...

159
00:11:30,516 --> 00:11:35,019
[nm]: How can you free yourself from suffering, when only suffering is necessary, basically?

160
00:11:36,164 --> 00:11:40,022
[nm]: Sorry, when only the necessity of suffering is your only criteria?

161
00:11:42,253 --> 00:11:47,213
[nm]: So, I don't know what to do in terms of freeing myself from suffering, but I'm doing all these things to free myself of suffering.

162
00:11:49,350 --> 00:11:52,829
[nm]: But you don't know how, where and why would those things free you from suffering.

163
00:11:53,526 --> 00:11:58,381
[nm]: You just hope that through doing these random things, the context of freeing from suffering will be reached.

164
00:12:07,710 --> 00:12:08,589
[nm]: So, that's what I mean,

165
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:15,252
[nm]: no amount of methods, techniques or whatever, like just through sheer doing, can suddenly bring the revelation.

166
00:12:16,059 --> 00:12:21,348
[nm]: Trying to discern revelation, the right view, that's what can bring the right view.

167
00:12:23,668 --> 00:12:26,004
[nm]: And then, whatever you do through it, will be right.

168
00:12:26,779 --> 00:12:28,089
[nm]: But not other way around.

169
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:36,541
[nm]: You're not going to concoct the right view through randomly doing these separate things, that then magically just create this Frankenstein of a view.

170
00:12:53,748 --> 00:12:58,294
[tn]: There's a difference between, like, my opinion and then the right view.

171
00:12:58,800 --> 00:12:59,648
[nm]: Yeah, absolutely.

172
00:12:59,657 --> 00:13:06,514
[nm]: Again, if you're unaware of the context of your own situation, as in fundamental context of: am I free from suffering?

173
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:08,169
[nm]: Am I not free from suffering?

174
00:13:08,178 --> 00:13:08,626
[nm]: That's it.

175
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:09,586
[nm]: That's the basis.

176
00:13:09,698 --> 00:13:11,689
[nm]: And you don't need to go anywhere further from that.

177
00:13:11,764 --> 00:13:17,024
[nm]: That can remain the criteria throughout, whether you're puthujjana or arya, until you become an arahant.

178
00:13:17,622 --> 00:13:19,252
[nm]: Am I completely free from suffering or not?

179
00:13:21,284 --> 00:13:33,026
[nm]: But if you're not aware of that, then, yeah, your opinions would be basically a secondary kind of induced points of view on account of taking your experience for granted.

180
00:13:33,794 --> 00:13:38,982
[nm]: So, instead of your opinions questioning your experience, your opinions are just being built on top of your experience.

181
00:13:40,368 --> 00:13:46,484
[nm]: So, that's what I mean, like, people would have these, like, genuine experiences of, you know, sudden peace or release or something, but instead of:

182
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:47,547
[nm]: Okay, that's good.

183
00:13:47,670 --> 00:13:56,640
[nm]: There is a hope that I can develop this peace, but instead of recognizing that that can only be developed through full understanding of the nature of it, they don't question it.

184
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:58,402
[nm]: They just take it as it happened.

185
00:13:58,409 --> 00:13:58,868
[nm]: That's it.

186
00:13:58,860 --> 00:14:00,507
[nm]: Now, it must be real forever.

187
00:14:00,510 --> 00:14:05,033
[nm]: So, now, it's just a question of, sort of, defending it, protecting it or prolonging it...

188
00:14:06,170 --> 00:14:13,108
[nm]: Through trying to manipulate the environment, and go on a longer retreat, and then do this, and avoid talking to people, and then... to not disturb your peace.

189
00:14:16,717 --> 00:14:20,086
[nm]: But you realize, what you are defending is not even your peace.

190
00:14:21,195 --> 00:14:31,298
[nm]: You're defending that experience as a whole, which, if you were to look closer, you would realize it has arisen on its own, with its own characteristics, and signs, and context.

191
00:14:31,908 --> 00:14:33,730
[nm]: And you just took it for granted that it's yours.

192
00:14:33,730 --> 00:14:34,185
[nm]: Why?

193
00:14:34,717 --> 00:14:36,219
[nm]: Because it was very agreeable to you.

194
00:14:37,147 --> 00:14:42,036
[nm]: That's why most people who even commit years and years to meditation, they end up meditating with their sensuality.

195
00:14:42,034 --> 00:14:45,206
[nm]: As in, sensuality is the base criteria for their meditation.

196
00:14:45,627 --> 00:14:47,382
[nm]: What is agreeable, what's disagreeable.

197
00:14:50,262 --> 00:14:54,388
[nm]: Now, you cannot... that is just a necessary way how you have to start.

198
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:58,413
[nm]: But one thing is to have that as a necessary basis.

199
00:14:58,420 --> 00:15:01,824
[nm]: In other words, puthujjana has to start somehow, and it's not going to be right.

200
00:15:02,749 --> 00:15:04,850
[nm]: But another thing is to never grow out of it.

201
00:15:21,581 --> 00:15:24,813
[tn]: So, how can... how can we know if we are making progress?

202
00:15:25,661 --> 00:15:28,525
[nm]: Again, context, whether you're free from suffering or not.

203
00:15:29,590 --> 00:15:38,635
[nm]: Is what you're doing... is all your experiences you had as a result of your, like, whatever, intense meditations and pondering on the teachings...

204
00:15:39,350 --> 00:15:44,491
[nm]: That's all fine, but overall, am I now more free from suffering than I was before?

205
00:15:45,770 --> 00:15:48,916
[nm]: Will I be more affected or will I be less affected?

206
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,934
[nm]: Or will I be affected at all?

207
00:15:51,282 --> 00:15:54,987
[nm]: By things that would... And again, oh, I'm not affected right now.

208
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:55,810
[nm]: No, but imagine.

209
00:15:55,810 --> 00:15:57,805
[nm]: Imagine your loved ones dying around you.

210
00:15:57,810 --> 00:16:03,606
[nm]: Imagine you losing your senses, your health, getting sick, loss of wealth, loss of home, loss of whatever.

211
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:06,809
[nm]: Imagine it and see, is there fear in regard to it?

212
00:16:07,147 --> 00:16:13,803
[nm]: If there is a fear in regard to it, if there is like: "oh, I don't want to look at this" you can't then at the same time say, oh, but I'm free from suffering.

213
00:16:14,102 --> 00:16:15,421
[nm]: Yeah, that's what I mean,

214
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:20,630
[nm]: if you start developing that context through that questioning, you're going to start developing self-honesty as well.

215
00:16:21,476 --> 00:16:24,870
[tn]: Because a lot of... you can ask a lot of people, do you suffer?

216
00:16:25,428 --> 00:16:25,739
[nm]: Yeah.

217
00:16:25,730 --> 00:16:28,059
[tn]: And a lot of people, lots of people will say...

218
00:16:28,102 --> 00:16:28,816
[nm]: No, I don't.

219
00:16:28,996 --> 00:16:29,792
[tn]: [?I don't have].

220
00:16:29,830 --> 00:16:35,563
[tn]: But it's more like, in the past, when I was a child, I didn't know what I was doing, I was suffering, things were new to me.

221
00:16:35,670 --> 00:16:35,977
[tn]: Sure.

222
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,379
[tn]: But now I'm older, I can deal with things much better.

223
00:16:38,379 --> 00:16:38,381
[nm]: Exactly.
[tn]: But now I'm older, I can deal with things much better.

224
00:16:38,381 --> 00:16:38,774
[nm]: Exactly.

225
00:16:38,816 --> 00:16:40,141
[tn]: So, I'm nibbāna.

226
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:40,500
[nm]: Yeah.

227
00:16:40,516 --> 00:16:42,253
[nm]: So, you need to upgrade your context.

228
00:16:42,884 --> 00:16:43,404
[nm]: That's what I mean.

229
00:16:44,573 --> 00:16:45,652
[nm]: Yeah, I don't suffer now.

230
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:46,667
[nm]: Okay, that's fine.

231
00:16:46,678 --> 00:16:47,773
[nm]: That's your first answer.

232
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:50,987
[nm]: Now, ask a further question: why am I not suffering?

233
00:16:51,467 --> 00:16:52,790
[nm]: Is it because I'm an arahant?

234
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:58,061
[nm]: Or is it because there's nothing currently inducing suffering in me?

235
00:16:59,522 --> 00:17:02,066
[nm]: If your answer is, oh, it's because I'm an arahant, great.

236
00:17:02,210 --> 00:17:04,372
[nm]: You don't need to do anything ever again.

237
00:17:05,572 --> 00:17:06,091
[nm]: You're done.

238
00:17:07,977 --> 00:17:09,549
[nm]: You wouldn't be even listening to this talk, then.

239
00:17:11,547 --> 00:17:19,661
[nm]: But if your answer is, well, you know, I probably still could suffer in some extreme scenarios,

240
00:17:20,258 --> 00:17:22,713
[nm]: Means you can't then say that you're free from nature of suffering.

241
00:17:23,490 --> 00:17:26,996
[nm]: Because there is no extreme scenario for somebody who is free from suffering.

242
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:38,715
[nm]: Somebody who is free from the nature of suffering, somebody who is free from liability to suffering, cannot suffer on any account of any particular suffering, big or small, extreme or not, he cannot suffer.

243
00:17:41,094 --> 00:17:45,981
[nm]: So, by keeping that context in the mind, you keep your practice along the right lines.

244
00:17:47,846 --> 00:17:49,385
[nm]: You won't stop making the effort,

245
00:17:49,824 --> 00:18:02,148
[nm]: You won't get complacent, nor will you get sort of deluded on account of your own, you know, attainments and whatnot, experiences you had, that then people told you there must have been that thing or this thing or whatever.

246
00:18:02,838 --> 00:18:06,601
[nm]: If somebody needs to tell you what that must have been, means you don't really know what it was.

247
00:18:07,524 --> 00:18:11,001
[nm]: If you don't know what it was, how can you say you're free from doubt in regard to it?

248
00:18:11,177 --> 00:18:13,021
[nm]: How can you say that you know that you know?

249
00:18:13,643 --> 00:18:14,848
[nm]: I know that I know.

250
00:18:15,371 --> 00:18:21,977
[nm]: Not through like some blind kind of religious fundamentalism, but just, no, genuinely I understand how it came to be.

251
00:18:22,482 --> 00:18:23,698
[nm]: I understand how it ceased.

252
00:18:23,691 --> 00:18:25,225
[nm]: I understand what it is.

253
00:18:25,387 --> 00:18:26,980
[nm]: I understand wholesome is wholesome.

254
00:18:28,893 --> 00:18:37,010
[nm]: No method or technique can teach you that, except your own effort and self-questioning and reflection with the guidance of the suttas and the Buddha's instruction.

